  "title": "The Least Uniquely Three-Colorable Integral Circulant with Clique Number Two",
  "batch_label": "53",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every positive integer n and every subset D of the proper positive divisors of n, let ICG_n(D) be the simple graph on Z_n in which distinct x,y are adjacent exactly when gcd(x-y,n) lies in D. Among graphs that are uniquely 3-colorable and have clique number 2, the least possible order is n=60. At that least order the complete classification by equality of labeled graphs is the single divisor set D={2,5}; its unique unordered color-class partition consists of the three residue classes modulo 3.",
